				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1505,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(LNGA): release scanned_extensions lock before aggregation loop\n\nLanguages.GetAll held the scanned_extensions mutex for the full\nduration of the multi-extension aggregation loop. Any other thread\nthat needed the same lock was blocked until the entire merge\ncompleted.\n\nFix: clone the map out of the lock immediately inside a short scope,\nrelease the lock, then run the aggregation over the owned clone.",
			"SHA": "1b1b92a350d566202daf453cd1eb35178e664fa5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T20:16:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1505,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(LNGF): replace hardcoded ProviderType::Hover with per-type match arms\n\nThe single $languageFeatures:registerProvider handler passed\nProviderType::Hover to RegisterProvider for every registration,\nso completion, definition, references, rename, and all other\nproviders were silently registered as Hover providers.\n\nCocoon sends separate notification method names for each provider\ntype (register_hover_provider, register_completion_item_provider,\netc.) with an object payload {language_selector, handle}. Mountain\nmust therefore match on each distinct method name and pass the\ncorresponding ProviderType. The id and selector fields are read\nfrom the object keys that Cocoon actually sends.",
			"SHA": "5be9c5c061c45d1312a8db96cc2b59a814bda07f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T18:20:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
